※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4482

※ Walking takes one dimension off an array at a time and stops when what is left
※ is what the parameter takes.  A dimension the type does not state is one the
※ walk cannot take off: what the answer is an array of is the shape that was
※ walked, and a shape nobody stated is one there is no room to answer with.

@[listable]
fn doubled(n: u8) → u8:
    n + n

fn walked(xs: u8⟦⟧) → u8:
    let d: u8⟦1⟧ = doubled(xs)
    d⟦0⟧

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let v: u8⟦2⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8⟧
    walked(v)
